CORRECTION (status, important): the researcher's '114-byte JS shell' at wid.world is not a client-rendered app. It is a domain-parking redirect. Every wid.world path returns script window.location.href='/lander', and /lander is a GoDaddy parking page (window._trfd ap:'parking', img1.wsimg.com/parking-lander). RDAP for wid.world shows:
- status 'auto renew period' plus client delete/renew/transfer/update prohibited;
- registration 2015-09-29;
- expiration now 2027-09-29;
- 'last changed' 2026-10-04T17:28Z;
- nameservers ns55/ns56.domaincontrol.com.
The domain appears to have lapsed around 2026-09-29 and is parked during the registrar's grace period. wir2026.wid.world is a CNAME to wid.world, so it is also down. Treat WID.world as OFFLINE or AT RISK and do not link to it until it is restored.

Other checks: the nature.com dc.rights is '2022 The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer Nature Limited' (not open access). The paper is Nature Sustainability 5(11), 931–938, online 2022-09-29. The Dropbox 'Codes & Data' zip still resolves (200, 26.8 MB). The data licence remains unknown, and the wid-r-tool GitHub repo licence is 'Other/NOASSERTION'.

The GOV.UK content API confirms first_published 2026-06-11, public_updated 2026-07-31, and the change note 'Updated the conversion factors 2026: flat file to correct a number of values that were initially reported as 0'. All three asset URLs return 200:
- full set: 2,109,334 bytes;
